+﻿//! AdiCode Blender Pro: expert skills, an in-Blender helper library
+//! (`adicode_blender`, installed into every Blender user modules folder),
+//! and the `blender_pro` tool (doctor / setup / helpers).
+
+use serde_json::{json, Value};
+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
+use std::process::Command;
+use std::time::Duration;
+
+#[cfg(windows)]
+use std::os::windows::process::CommandExt;
+
+pub(crate) const HELPERS: &str = include_str!("blender_helpers.py");
+
+pub(crate) const SKILL_CORE: &str = r#"Goal: production-quality Blender results, verified visually. Tools: blender_* (MCP for Blender: get_scene_info, execute_blender_code, look, search_assets, import_asset, generate_3d), blender_pro (doctor, setup, helpers), comfyui_* (local AI images/textures/image-to-3D on the RTX GPU), pc_PowerShell (headless renders), context7 (Blender Python API docs).
+
+0. Start
+- blender_get_addon_status. If Blender is not reachable: blender_pro action=doctor, then tell the user exactly what to click (Blender open, N panel -> MCP for Blender -> Start/Connect, port 9876).
+- First code call in every session: import adicode_blender as A, importlib; importlib.reload(A); print(A.help()). If import fails: blender_pro action=install_helpers.
+- Load the specialised skill too: blender-model (modeling/materials/assets) or blender-anim (animation/rigging/physics/camera).
+
+1. Plan before code (2-5 lines): deliverable (still, turntable, animation, game asset), style (realistic, stylised, low-poly), real-world scale in metres, shot/camera, time budget. Unclear requests: propose 2-3 concrete directions.
+- Order: blockout at true scale -> silhouette check from camera -> forms -> materials -> lighting -> detail -> render. Never jump to details on a bad blockout.
+- Naming: GEO-, MAT-, LGT-, CAM-, RIG-, CTRL- prefixes, collections per part. Keep modifiers non-destructive until the end.
+
+2. Code rules (Blender 4.2-5.x)
+- One logical step per execute_blender_code call (< ~120 lines), print a compact result, check it before the next step.
+- Check renders small and fast: A.render_settings('EEVEE', res=(1280,720), quality='draft') (quality only draft|high|final), A.render('check.png', scale=40-50), then blender_look image=<path> max_size=640. Finals later with quality='high'/'final'.
+- Prefer data API / bmesh / A.* helpers over bpy.ops; if an operator is needed use A.op(bpy.ops.x.y, objects=[...]) (context override). Never rely on the user's selection or mode; return to OBJECT mode.
+- Apply scale (A.apply_transforms) before bevel, booleans, physics, rigging and export.
+- 5.x API: EEVEE engine id 'BLENDER_EEVEE' (A.render_settings handles it), Principled sockets 'Emission Color', 'Coat Weight', 'Subsurface Weight', 'Transmission Weight'; layered actions (use A._fcurves(obj)); shade_smooth_by_angle; geometry nodes interface via ng.interface.new_socket. Unsure about an API: context7 'blender python api' or introspect (bpy.types.X.bl_rna.properties.keys()) instead of guessing.
+- Long work (renders > 30 s, bakes, simulations): save the file (A.save()), then run headless via pc_PowerShell Start-Process "blender.exe" -ArgumentList '-b','<file.blend>','-E','CYCLES','-a' with a log file; poll the log. MCP calls time out after ~55 s.
+
+3. Verification loop (mandatory, never report done without it)
+- After every major step: blender_look (viewport/camera image) and/or A.render('check.png', scale=40) and look at it; A.quality() for meshes.
+- Fix what you see: floating objects, intersections, wrong scale, flat lighting, noisy or blown-out render, uniform plastic look, stretched textures.
+- Animation: A.contact_sheet() at 5 frames, check poses, arcs, contact with the ground, no popping.
+
+3b. Reference image (rebuild from a picture) - mandatory loop
+- A.measure_ref(path): silhouette aspect, width profile, dominant colours. Use these numbers for proportions and base colours, never eyeball them.
+- A.ref_camera(path, view='persp'|'front'|'side'|'top'): render aspect = image aspect, reference as camera background. Match the camera first (angle, lens) until the blockout overlaps the picture.
+- Build: decompose into 3-8 main parts -> one script for the blockout at true scale -> A.compare() -> fix the hints -> forms -> A.compare() -> materials (colours from measure_ref) -> A.compare().
+- A.compare() returns iou, shape_iou, verdict, hints and a composite PNG (reference | render | overlay: yellow match, red missing, blue extra). Look at the composite (blender_look or open the PNG) every round.
+- At least 3 compare rounds. Not done before shape_iou >= 0.85 (stylised/organic: >= 0.75) and main_color_diff <= 0.15; report the final scores. Organic hero shapes: blender_generate_3d from the reference as base mesh, then compare and refine.
+- Multi-view references: A.ortho_views() and compare front/side/top separately.
+
+4. Quality bar ('krass' instead of 'okay')
+- Bevel every hard edge (A.hard_surface), weighted normals; organic forms use subdivision (A.organic). Silhouette must read from the camera.
+- Fast realistic materials: A.preset(kind, color=None, roughness=None) with brass|gold|copper|steel|chrome|aluminum|iron|glass|frosted_glass|tinted_glass|plastic|rubber|ceramic|wood|dark_wood|fabric|concrete (wood = procedural grain, A.procedural(..., kind='wood')).
+- Materials always vary: roughness/colour variation (A.procedural), bump or normal map, edge wear/dirt for realism. Real textures: Poly Haven/ambientCG via blender_search_assets + A.pbr_textures(folder).
+- Lighting: A.studio('three_point'|'rim'|'soft') or an HDRI (Poly Haven) + one key light; AgX view transform; shadows grounded (A.floor, contact shadows).
+- Camera: A.camera(objs, lens, angle=(azimuth, elevation), margin=1.1) frames the whole bounding box (tall objects included) and points at it; lights from A.studio also aim at the target. 35-85 mm, rule of thirds, depth of field on hero shots (cam.data.dof.use_dof, focus_object), slight elevation.
+- Render: EEVEE for previews, Cycles GPU OptiX for finals (A.gpu(), A.render_settings('CYCLES', quality='high')), denoise on, motion blur for animation.
+
+5. Assets and AI (big quality boost, use them)
+- Poly Haven HDRIs/textures/models (free, CC0), Sketchfab, Poly Pizza through blender_search_assets/blender_import_asset.
+- Complex organic hero props/characters: blender_generate_3d (Hunyuan3D/Tripo/Rodin) or local ComfyUI image-to-3D, then A.cleanup, decimate/remesh, UV, scale to real size, re-light. Concept images/seamless textures: comfyui_generate_image.
+
+6. Deliver: save .blend + renders/videos to PlazCode-Shared/blender-out (A.save, A.render, A.render_video), export glb/fbx (A.export). Report file paths, what was built, render settings, and next improvement ideas."#;
+
+pub(crate) const SKILL_MODEL: &str = r#"Modeling, materials and assets for high-quality results.
+
+Workflow
+1. Reference: ask for or generate (comfyui_generate_image) a reference/concept; derive proportions in metres (door 2.0 m, table 0.75 m, human 1.75 m, car 4.5 m).
+2. Blockout from primitives (A.primitive(kind, size=..., radius=..., depth=..., radius2=...) for cylinders/cones/tori at exact dimensions) at true scale; check silhouette from the camera (A.camera + blender_look).
+3. Primary -> secondary -> tertiary forms. Detail density must vary (calm areas vs. detailed areas).
+4. Topology: quads on deforming/curved surfaces, ngons only on flat faces, support loops or bevels for crisp subdivided edges.
+5. UV (A.uv_unwrap) only when image textures or baking are needed; procedural materials use Object coordinates.
+6. A.quality(): non_manifold_edges 0 for booleans/3D print, scale_applied True, no loose verts, normals outward (A.cleanup).
+
+Hard surface (vehicles, weapons, props, architecture, robots)
+- Booleans (modifier, EXACT solver, cutters in a hidden collection; Bool Tool extension installed by blender_pro setup) -> Bevel (angle limit 30 deg, harden normals) -> Weighted Normal (A.hard_surface).
+- Mirror for symmetry, Array + Curve for repeated parts (chains, treads, rails), Solidify for panels, Screw for lathe parts (wheels, bottles), curves with bevel depth for cables/pipes, Skin modifier for frames.
+- Panel lines: boolean cuts with small bevels; add greebles via geometry nodes instancing (A.scatter on a selection) instead of copy-paste.
+
+Organic (characters, creatures, plants, rocks, terrain)
+- Base mesh: subdivided cubes, Skin modifier, or metaballs -> Voxel Remesh -> Subdivision (A.organic) -> displacement with noise textures for rocks/terrain.
+- Characters: prefer generate_3d (Hunyuan3D/Tripo/Rodin) or a ready asset for realism, then retopo: Quadriflow (bpy.ops.object.quadriflow_remesh via A.op) or Decimate, shrinkwrap details.
+- Vegetation and scattering: geometry nodes (A.scatter with density, random scale and rotation), several variants, never identical copies.
+
+Procedural / geometry nodes
+- Use nodes for anything repetitive (buildings, fences, crowds of rocks, cables). Keep parameters exposed so you can iterate quickly.
+
+Materials (Principled BSDF, linear values)
+- Never pure black/white albedo (0.03-0.9). Metals: metallic 1, roughness 0.15-0.45, coloured base (gold 1.0/0.71/0.29, copper 0.95/0.64/0.54, steel 0.56/0.57/0.58). Plastics 0.3-0.6 roughness, rubber 0.8-0.9, glass transmission 1 roughness 0-0.05 IOR 1.45-1.5, car paint coat weight 1, skin subsurface weight 0.1-0.25.
+- Realism comes from variation: A.procedural (noise/voronoi/wave -> colour + roughness + bump), AO/pointiness edge wear, dirt in cavities, scratches via stretched noise.
+- Image textures: A.pbr_textures(folder) sets sRGB for colour and Non-Color for data maps; real textures from Poly Haven via blender_search_assets.
+
+AI-generated meshes (generate_3d / ComfyUI Hunyuan3D, TRELLIS)
+- Import -> A.cleanup(obj) -> Decimate (ratio so tris fit the budget) or Remesh -> smart UV -> bake or re-material -> scale to real size -> origin to base -> sits on the floor.
+- Budgets: hero render 100k-1M tris fine; game asset 2k-30k tris + baked normal map; Roblox: < 10k tris per mesh, FBX export with applied scale.
+
+Presentation
+- A.floor + A.studio + A.camera(lens=50..85) + AgX; render a turntable for models (A.orbit + render_video)."#;
+
+pub(crate) const SKILL_ANIM: &str = r#"Animation, rigging, physics and camera work that looks professional.
+
+Plan
+- Shot list with durations in seconds, fps (24 film, 30 web, 60 game), frame range. Write the beats: anticipation -> action -> follow-through -> settle.
+- Block first with CONSTANT interpolation (stepped poses on key frames), review with A.contact_sheet, then switch to BEZIER (A.set_interp) and polish.
+
+12 principles applied
+- Slow in/out (BEZIER auto-clamped, easing), arcs (move along curves, A.follow_path), anticipation (counter-move 4-8 frames before), follow-through and overlap (offset child/secondary parts 2-4 frames), squash and stretch preserving volume (A.bounce), secondary action (A.shake noise for breathing/hover/idle), timing (fast = few frames, heavy = slow ease), exaggeration for stylised work.
+
+Techniques
+- Keys: A.key(obj, frame, location=..., rotation_euler=..., scale=...). Loops: A.loop (Cycles F-modifier). Organic motion: A.shake (Noise F-modifier). Layering: NLA strips (A.nla_push).
+- Drivers for mechanics (wheel rotation = distance / radius, pistons, gears), constraints: Track To/Damped Track (eyes, cameras, turrets), Child Of (pick up/hand over), Follow Path, Limit Rotation, Copy Rotation for retargeting.
+- Shape keys for faces/morphs; drivers on shape keys for blinks and expressions.
+- Mechanical/procedural motion: geometry nodes with simulation zones, or drivers using frame (#frame) expressions.
+
+Characters
+- Own rig: A.human_rig() creates a Rigify human (IK/FK, foot roll). Fit the metarig to the mesh (A.human_rig(generate=False), edit bones), then generate, then A.skin(mesh, rig) automatic weights; test extreme poses and fix weights.
+- Realistic motion fast: Mixamo (auto-rig + motion library, FBX download; use browser_* if the user is logged in, or ask the user to download), CMU/Bandai BVH mocap, video mocap (FreeMoCap, Rokoko Video, Move.ai) and text-to-motion AI (e.g. NVIDIA Kimodo, Motion Gen addon, MotionGPT/HY-Motion) that export BVH/FBX -> A.import_motion(path) -> retarget (Copy Rotation constraints or the Rokoko/Auto-Rig Pro remap addons) -> clean feet sliding -> layer hand-keyed polish on top in the NLA.
+- Walk cycle: 24-32 frames per cycle at 24 fps, contact-down-passing-up poses, hips move in a figure-8, arms opposite to legs, A.loop.
+
+Physics and FX
+- Rigid body (collapse, dominoes), cloth (flags, capes; pin group), Mantaflow fluid/smoke/fire, particles; bake before rendering (A.bake_physics) with the exact frame range; check every 10th frame.
+- Glow: emission strength 5-50 + compositor Glare (bloom); volumetric light via Principled Volume in a world/box; motion blur on.
+
+Camera
+- Motivated moves: slow push-in, orbit (A.orbit), follow with Damped Track; ease every camera key. Lens 24-35 for action, 50 for neutral, 85+ for close-ups. Subtle handheld A.shake(cam, 'rotation_euler', 0.004-0.015, 20). Depth of field with focus_object. Cuts: several cameras bound to markers.
+
+Review and render
+- A.contact_sheet() and blender_look while scrubbing frames: no intersections, feet planted, no popping, readable silhouettes.
+- Preview: EEVEE, 50% resolution, A.render_video('preview.mp4', scale=50) for short clips, otherwise headless.
+- Final: Cycles GPU (A.gpu) or EEVEE high, PNG sequence for long renders (resume-safe), headless blender -b file.blend -a via Start-Process with a log, then MP4 via ffmpeg."#;
